Z||000011||2FAST4U||12-25-1999||08:13 PM||||It is a really great Christmas indeed. I got a 50" TV, a really great NHRA jacket with red and yellow flames, NASCAR Greatest Races book, a Lava Lamp (giving away my age), some clothes, the biggest bottle of wine I've ever seen, urethane mounts and bushings for my 85 GT, and a real world class hangover from last nights Christmas Eve party!<P>I hope everyone was as blessed with great gifts, great friends, and great happiness as I have been this year.<P>MERRY CHRISTMAS and HAPPY NEW YEAR!!!!!!<P>2FAST4U<BR>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000012||mshill||12-25-1999||11:27 PM||||<BR>2FAST4U, my kids had to have a lava lamp this year. I think it is pretty cool that they are coming back.<P>Since a few years ago my wife and I don't buy each other presents anymore, so she bought herself a DVD player (gotta love that!!!) and I bought myself the 86GT last weekend.<P>My 86SE has also given me a present... instead of the monthly coolant leak I got a plugged exhaust (cat of muffler).<P>I think the 86SE (aka Swiss Cheese) is just begging for a rebuild to start off the new year.  Looks like it is going to get it.<p>[This message has been edited by mshill (edited 12-25-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000013||DJRice||12-26-1999||10:44 AM||||I got a DVD Player and some 3 movies to get started with.  I also got a nice tool assortment and some clothes from my parents.  <P>My dads 86 4 banger Fiero got an engine removal (on Christmas Eve) because of a broken weld on the engine cradle.  Turns out we had a crack in the Exhaust Manifold too.<P>Again, Happy Holidays!||||reg||1
